# What goes into the Docker build context.
#
# Default-deny: ignore EVERYTHING and explicitly include only the files
# the Dockerfile actually COPYs. Cuts the build context from ~1.2 GB
# (mostly the desktop installer artifacts under bin/, dist/, build/, and
# the samples + docs site that are unrelated to the container) down to
# only the code the image needs.

*

# Engine + web app source — what `COPY app/` and `COPY web/` consume.
!app/
!web/

# Bundled assets the engine reads at runtime: selfextract_stub.exe (for
# Stone .exe self-compile output) and any icons / fonts that happen to
# end up referenced. Trim aggressively below.
!resources/

# Container-specific files at the repo root.
!Dockerfile
!docker/
!requirements.txt
!alembic.ini

# Pruning inside the included trees — Python build artifacts, editor
# state, and the giant resources/ subdirs we don't need.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# resources/ — keep stubs + fonts (small), drop heavyweight installer
# imagery and screenshots that only the desktop build / docs site use.
resources/screenshots/
resources/installer/
resources/icons/*.psd
resources/**/*.bak

# Anything explicitly excluded above gets re-banned even if a parent was
# allowlisted with `!`. Belt-and-suspenders for clarity.
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
docs/
samples/
bin/
wheels/
build/
dist/
logs/
tools/

# OS junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# README and license aren't COPYed into the image (they're for the GitHub
# repo page); skip them too.
README.md
LICENSE
*.md
docker-compose.yml
